course: dictionary
lesson: 4466
title: The hare that runs fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hare is a wild animal like a large rabbit, with long ears and long, strong back legs that help it run very fast. «The hare shot across the field before the dog could catch up.» The clues shot across and before the dog could catch up tell you the hare is quick.
explain: Hares and rabbits look alike, but they are not the same. Hares are bigger, and their ears are longer with black tips. «Hares live above ground in a shallow nest called a form.» Rabbits often live in burrows underground, so this sentence helps you tell the two apart.
explain: Hare is also part of some phrases. «As mad as a March hare» means very wild and silly, not a real animal. «The Tortoise and the Hare» is a story, so ask what the sentence is about before you decide if hare means the animal.
fact: A hare is a wild animal like a large rabbit, with long ears and long, strong back legs.
fact: Hares are bigger than rabbits, and they have longer ears with black tips.
fact: Hares live above ground in a shallow nest called a form, while many rabbits live in burrows underground.
fact: Baby hares are called leverets, and they are born with fur and open eyes.
fact: Mountain and snowshoe hares turn white in winter, which helps them hide in the snow.
exercise: «The hare shot across the field before the dog could catch up.» What is a hare? | A kind of bird that cannot fly | A small sweet made of sugar | *A wild animal like a large rabbit, with long ears and strong back legs | A tall tree in a forest
exercise: How is a hare different from a rabbit? | It has no ears at all | It is smaller than a mouse | *It is bigger and has longer ears with black tips | It lives in the sea
exercise: «Baby hares are called leverets, and they are born with fur and open eyes.» Find and copy one word for a baby hare. | eyes | fur | *leverets | hares
test: Why do mountain hares turn white in winter? | Because they are cold and need a coat | *To hide in the snow | To keep cool in summer | To look like a cloud
test: In the story «The Tortoise and the Hare», what does the story teach? | *Slow and steady wins the race | Rabbits are better than hares | Sleeping is good for you | Fast runners always win
exam: Which phrase uses hare to mean wild and silly? | as wet as a fish | *as mad as a March hare | as fast as a train | as quiet as a mouse
